    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nAs tab characters take up more than one visible column on the screen, the handling of gen_path.angle should multiply tab characters by their width in visible columns.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen a file that uses tabs, e.g. Go code. Scroll to a position that is indented using as many tabs as possible (for greater effect), observe where the line animation goes.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe line animation ends at the column that the character count at the target position implies, not at the visible target position taking into account visible tab width.",
